## Reporting status (REQUIRED)

You report status by calling these CLI commands from inside the tmux window.
They write atomically to the shared dashboard. Skipping them makes the
operator's cockpit blind to your progress.

| When | Run |
|---|---|
| Starting a turn after reading the prompt | `agent-status {slug} WORKING "<one-line summary>"` |
| You need a user decision but are not fully blocked | `agent-status {slug} NEEDS_FEEDBACK "<the question>"` |
| You cannot proceed without input or access | `agent-mark-as-blocked {slug} "<what is blocking>"` |
| You believe the task is ready for review | `agent-status {slug} READY "<what you did>"` |
| You finished the task | `agent-mark-done {slug} "<summary>"` |
| You hit an unrecoverable issue | `agent-status {slug} FAILED "<what failed>"` |

Bump `WORKING` summaries whenever you switch to a substantively different
activity ("running tests", "investigating null check", "drafting PR
description"). The cockpit flags `WORKING` rows that haven't moved in 30
minutes as `[stale]`.

## Blocking rules

Use `agent-mark-as-blocked` (which rings the operator's bell) for hard
blocks only:

- a decision you can't make without the user (policy, naming, semantics);
- missing access (token, env, service);
- broken or contradictory instructions in the prompt.

Use `agent-status … NEEDS_FEEDBACK` for softer asks that can wait a few
minutes — design questions, "is this approach OK?", code-review-style
checkpoints. NEEDS_FEEDBACK does NOT ring the bell.

## Git rules

- Work happens in the worktree on `agent/{slug}/<repo>`. Never check out
  another branch in the worktree.
- Commit often with descriptive messages; do NOT amend pushed commits.
- Do not force-push, rebase shared history, or merge to base branch
  yourself.
- If your work is ready for a PR, mention it in the summary; the user
  opens the PR.

## Task source and handoff

- The **operator's first message** in this conversation is the
  authoritative description of the task. There is no `prompt.md`.
- `{workspace_path}/.agent/HANDOFF.md` is the running record you maintain
  for the operator. Update its sections as work progresses; the operator
  reads it when picking the work up after a break.

